[Music]  [Applause]  welcome to CBS this morning you know rod  Rosen I was probably standing there  thinking if I move a muscle the  late-night comedians are gonna talk  about me and others and say I don't know  him never met him but it didn't look  like he wanted to be there no it's like  not to say anything but you say  everything and I'm gonna start by saying  this which is Anthony Mason is here  because Norah O'Donnell is off  Republicans say it is time to put the  Russia investigation in the past  Democrats have a different plan now that  the Robert Muller's report is out in the  public President Trump claims total  exoneration and Russia's government is  dismissing Muller's findings but the  special counsels 448 page report details  the president's repeated efforts to  stymie the investigation and how he was  stopped by the people around him mother  found no collusion with Russian  interfering with the election but he did  not decide the question of obstruction  of justice according to the report if  Muller's team could have definitely said  the president did not commit a crime  they would have Paula rediscovered this  investigation from the very beginning  she's at the White House with the latest  on this story Paula there is a lot to  discuss today good morning Gail there is  so much to discuss but of course we have  to make clear the president has not been  charged with any crime but according to  Robert Muller it's not for lack of  trying the special counsels report  yesterday laid out how often the people  around the president need to protect him  from his worst instincts in yesterday in  a press conference his Attorney General  William Barre often sounded like a  defense attorney offering a very  understanding interpretation of the  president's actions in May 2017  president Trump slumped in his chair in  the Oval Office and said robert muller  would be the end of his presidency  according to the special counsels  blockbuster report muller describes for  the first time an angry president  reacting to the appointment of a special  counsel i'm effed he told his then  attorney general jeff sessions who had  just relayed the news this is the worst  thing that has ever happened to me  but yesterday the president declared  victory over the investigations findings  i'm having a good day too  it was called no collusion no  obstruction  but that's not exactly what the report  said muller concluded the president did  not coordinate with Russia's efforts to  interfere in the 2016 election they have  one of the great memories of all time  though mr. Trump's written answers  surrounding Russia were considered  inadequate in nearly three dozen  instances the president said he could  not remember events Muller's account  details roughly two years of chaos in  which mr. Trump struggled to respond to  the Russia investigation and cites 10  episodes that could possibly constitute  obstruction in one example the report  states that in June 2017 the president  called former White House Counsel Don  Magan at least twice and told him to  have the special counsel fired Magan  recalled feeling trapped because he did  not plan to follow the president's  directive but did not know what he would  say the next time the president called  Magan decided he needed to resign the  report says the president's efforts to  influence the investigation were mostly  unsuccessful but that is largely because  the persons who surrounded the president  declined to carry out orders or cede to  his requests the special counsel  concluded it could not exonerate the  President on whether he obstructed  justice and it was Muller's boss  Attorney General William Barr who  cleared the President on that question  in a press conference yesterday Barr  defended his handling of the  investigation so what did you say to  people on both sides of the aisle  concerned that you were trying to  protect the statements about his is his  sincere beliefs are recognized in the  report that there was substantial  evidence for that so I'm not sure what  your basis is for saying that I am being  generous to the president the report  revealed prosecutors are pursuing 14  other matters referred by the special  counsel only two of those are known to  the public the investigation of Michael  Cohen as well as a separate  investigation into a former Obama  administration official but those 12  other mystery investigations ensure that  even though this report has been  submitted Muller shadow will continue to  loom large over this White House Anthony  Paula thanks

